# AI Detection Service — environment configuration
#
# Copy to .env in this directory and fill in the values you have. Every key below is
# optional: the pipeline runs deterministically without any of them, and each unset
# key disables exactly one escalation path rather than breaking the service.
#
# On production this file is loaded by systemd via
#   EnvironmentFile=/var/www/avar/src/backend/ai-detection-service/.env
# systemd parsing rules: no spaces around '=', no shell expansion ($VAR is literal),
# surrounding quotes are stripped. Restart the unit after editing — values are read at
# process start:
#   systemctl restart avar-detection.service

# --- Layer 3: third-party AI detection (escalated only for QUARANTINE cases) ---
# Without these, Layer 3 returns QUARANTINE and the submission goes to a judge.
HIVE_AI_API_KEY=
OPTIC_API_KEY=
SIGHTENGINE_USER=
SIGHTENGINE_SECRET=

# --- Vision arbiter: RAW-JPG linkage tie-breaker (Google Gemini) ---
# Consulted ONLY when geometric verification cannot decide — frames with too little
# texture to yield keypoints (fog, minimalism, long exposures, night sky). It can
# confirm linkage but never reject a submission, and it fails open on any API error.
#
# Unset means the arbiter is inert: linkage stays fully deterministic and undecidable
# cases go to a judge instead. Expect it to fire on a small minority of submissions.
#
# Get a key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Vision model used by the arbiter. Must support image input and responseSchema.
# Optional — defaults to DEFAULT_MODEL in app/services/vision_arbiter.py when unset.
#
# Google retires models, and a retired model still appears in ListModels while failing
# on use with HTTP 404. Because the arbiter fails open, a stale name here disables the
# feature silently — so if the log shows "set GEMINI_MODEL to a current vision model",
# this is the setting to change; no code deploy needed.
#
# Verified working 2026-08-07 with this service's exact request: gemini-3.6-flash,
# gemini-3.5-flash, gemini-3.1-flash-lite, gemini-flash-latest.
# List what your key can reach:
#   curl -s -H "x-goog-api-key: $GEMINI_API_KEY" \
#     https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models | grep '"name"'
GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# --- Infrastructure ---
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/0
